<%# THE PAGE IS DARK BEFORE ITS STYLESHEET SAYS SO. Three parser-blocking
    scripts load ahead of the stylesheet, and until it lands the browser
    paints its default canvas: every navigation flashed one fully white frame
    in Firefox (2026-09-26). Declared in the head, ahead of every script, the
    canvas is dark from the first paint. A scheme, not a colour: the skin's
    colours stay the formant tokens'. The historical interface is upstream's
    light one and draws no scheme (test/functional/modulation_color_scheme_test.rb). %>
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
